preConditionHook:
// Brooks's permission to reverse: the last position closed as a LOSER within
// a bar or two of being entered, and the exit was just now. A gate only --
// the direction of the re-entry comes from whatever entry rule shares the
// pane, which is why both sides carry the same text.
//
// It is LastTradeCooldown's condition in the opposite sense PLUS the term
// that makes it a different rule: the losing trade must have been
// SHORT-LIVED. All three position accessors are measured (the
// positionprofit/totaltrades and barssinceexit register rows):
// PositionProfit(1) is the most recently CLOSED position net of the full
// round turn, ctx.BarsSinceExit() is EL's BarsSinceExit(1) -- 0 on the exit's
// own fill bar, counting up from there -- and TotalTrades is already
// incremented at that bar's close.
//
// THE HOLDING PERIOD IS NOT AN ACCESSOR, in either library. BarsSinceEntry
// answers 0 while flat (measured -- never a -1 sentinel), so once the trade
// is closed it cannot say how long it was open. It is reconstructed here, in
// the same three statements in BOTH twins, from the two values that ARE
// measured: carry the previous bar's MarketPosition and BarsSinceEntry, and
// on the bar the position goes flat the trade lasted prevBse + 1 bars -- the
// entry filled at the entry bar's open (BarsSinceEntry = 0 at that bar's
// close) and the exit filled at this bar's open. This is a reconstruction of
// an ELAPSED-BAR count, not of per-position P&L: ctx.MaxPositionProfit() and
// ctx.PositionProfit() are still used for anything about money, never
// emulated. A reversal never passes through flat so it cannot be mistaken
// for an exit, and the rule requires MarketPosition() == 0 in any case.
//
// haveHeld keeps the warm-up honest: lastHeld starts at 0, which would read
// as the quickest possible trade, so nothing fires until a position has
// actually closed.
if (prevMp != 0 && ctx.MarketPosition() == 0) {
    lastHeld = prevBse + 1;
    haveHeld = true;
}
reenterNow = ctx.MarketPosition() == 0 && ctx.TotalTrades() > 0
    && el_lt(ctx.PositionProfit(1), 0.0)
    && el_le((double)ctx.BarsSinceExit(), reentryBars)
    && haveHeld && el_le((double)lastHeld, quickBars);
prevMp = ctx.MarketPosition();
prevBse = ctx.BarsSinceEntry();
